details.image_prompt:
{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition is centered with generous negative space, captured from a 3/4 overhead angle (40°) to display the height and volume of the ingredients. The focus is sharp on the foreground sandwich, with the second plate softly blurred in the background, creating a shallow depth of field. Soft natural light flows from a window on the left, casting gentle, natural shadows across the scene. The setting features a rustic, aged oak wood tabletop with visible wood grain and faint knife marks. Two slices of dense, toasted whole-grain bread are laid flat on matte ceramic plates. Each slice is topped with a vibrant layer of fresh, peppery baby arugula, followed by a generous, rustic scoop of creamy chicken salad. The salad reveals a textured mix of tender, flaked chicken breast, crisp diced green celery, halved ruby-red grapes with glossy skins, and rough-chopped toasted walnuts, all lightly bound by a creamy Greek yogurt and Dijon dressing. A stray walnut piece and a few fallen arugula leaves rest on the wood surface near the plates. A stainless steel fork with a slight sheen rests casually on the linen napkin beside the front plate. The presentation is authentic and home-cooked, featuring a tiny, realistic drip of mustard-yogurt dressing on the rim of the plate and slightly asymmetric ingredient placement. The color palette is warm and inviting, dominated by earthy browns, deep greens, and jewel-toned reds. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene feels lived-in and cozy, capturing the moment just after preparation. Slight natural imperfections like a crumb trail or a misplaced grape ensure an authentic, non-commercial feel. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry, no artificial lighting, no hands, no text."
}
